  "tagline": "Embeddable C++ graph database library from Sparsity Technologies, refocused on embedded and mobile.",
  "description": "Sparksee (formerly DEX) is a commercial, embeddable graph database library written in C++ and spun out of the Universitat Politecnica de Catalunya. It stores labeled, attributed multigraphs with bitmap-based structures for compact storage and fast neighbor operations, and exposes native APIs for Java, .NET, C++, Python and Objective-C. Since version 6.0 (2021) it has focused on embedded and mobile devices. The vendor site is still up, but there is no public sign of releases after 6.0, so treat it as a niche, slow-moving option.",
